# ★ All text files are stored and checked out as LF.
#   The Git used on Windows here has core.autocrlf=true globally, so without
#   this file a checkout rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF even though
#   the committed blobs are LF. gofmt then reports every Go file as "not
#   formatted" on Windows, and shell scripts lose their shebang on Unix —
#   failures that have nothing to do with the code.
#   `eol=lf` in .gitattributes outranks core.autocrlf / core.eol and applies
#   to this repository only: no global git config is modified. `text=auto`
#   keeps Git from trying to normalize binary payloads.

* text=auto eol=lf

# CMD batch files are the one exception: they genuinely need CRLF if added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let text=auto guess wrong about binary payloads.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.wasm binary
